<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giorgione</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1477–1510</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Giorgio da Castelfranco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giorgione was a Venetian painter of the High <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> from Castelfranco <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a>. Very few works are securely attributed to him, among them The Tempest and the Castelfranco altarpiece, but his poetic landscapes, soft modelling and enigmatic subjects transformed Venetian painting. He worked with the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titian">Titian</a> on the frescoes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fondaco-dei-tedeschi">Fondaco dei Tedeschi</a> and died of plague in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giorgione.jpg" alt="Giorgione" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgione · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Self_portrait,_by_Giorgio_da_Castelfranco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
